I've left out the `http-client` import and the enrichment fetch. The node's `with` clause grants only `wasi:clocks/wall-clock@0.2.0`, and that clause is its entire authority. Adding the import ahead of the graph definition would make the component exceed its declared grant. Sending the input's text to an outside endpoint whose result is then thrown away would add data egress without changing the output. Once the graph definition grants `http-client`, the import can be added through that change.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{tick, run-info};

    import wasi:clocks/wall-clock@0.2.0;

    export run: func(tick: tick) -> run-info;
}
```

